# Alternative sans API : renommer en collect.yml, désactiver pages.yml pour éviter
# qu'un déploiement d'interface seul remplace le relevé publié.
name: Collecte par lots et publication
on:
  workflow_dispatch:
    inputs:
      series:
        description: IDs séparés par des virgules (recherche neuve seulement)
        default: '714,5350'
        required: true
permissions:
  contents: write
  pages: write
  id-token: write
concurrency:
  group: springer-pages
  cancel-in-progress: false
jobs:
  collect:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    timeout-minutes: 20
    environment:
      name: github-pages
      url: ${{ steps.deployment.outputs.page_url }}
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
        with:
          ref: ${{ github.event.repository.default_branch }}
          fetch-depth: 0
      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4
        with:
          node-version: 22
          cache: npm
      - run: npm ci
      - name: Charger la reprise durable
        run: |
          mkdir -p data
          if git ls-remote --exit-code --heads origin collector-state >/dev/null; then
            git fetch origin collector-state
            git show origin/collector-state:state.json > data/state.json
          fi
      - name: Collecter un lot
        id: collect
        env:
          SPRINGER_COLLECTION_ENABLED: ${{ vars.SPRINGER_COLLECTION_ENABLED }}
          COLLECTOR_USER_AGENT: ${{ vars.COLLECTOR_USER_AGENT }}
          SERIES_IDS: ${{ inputs.series }}
          MAX_PAGES: '40'
        run: npm run collect -- --run
      - name: Enregistrer le point de reprise (pas un cache)
        if: always() && steps.collect.outcome != 'skipped'
        run: |
          if [ ! -f data/state.json ]; then exit 1; fi
          git config user.name github-actions[bot]
          git config user.email github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com
          if git show-ref --verify --quiet refs/remotes/origin/collector-state; then
            git worktree add --detach /tmp/springer-state origin/collector-state
          else
            git worktree add -b collector-state /tmp/springer-state
          fi
          cp data/state.json /tmp/springer-state/state.json
          cd /tmp/springer-state
          git add state.json
          if ! git diff --cached --quiet; then git commit -m 'Enregistrer la progression Springer'; fi
          git push origin HEAD:refs/heads/collector-state
      - run: npm run build
      - uses: actions/configure-pages@v5
      - uses: actions/upload-pages-artifact@v3
        with:
          path: dist
      - uses: actions/deploy-pages@v4
        id: deployment
